.\" rmdir.1 -- maux's rmdir(1), in the V7 man(1) shape. An
.\" original page (this project's own text, not copied from a
.\" historic rmdir(1)), so it carries no third-party notice --
.\" MIT like the code, same posture as env.1. Rendered at build
.\" time to build/man/RMDIR.TXT and staged on the play image as
.\" /usr/man/RMDIR: `more /usr/man/RMDIR`.
.TH RMDIR 1 "September 14, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
rmdir \- remove empty directories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rmdir
[
.B \-p
]
.I dir
...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Rmdir
removes the directory entry named by each
.I dir
operand, in order. Each one must already be empty; ProDOS's own
DESTROY call refuses a non-empty directory. A
.I dir
that cannot be removed is reported and skipped;
.I rmdir
continues with the remaining operands.
.TP
.B \-p
Also remove each pathname component of
.I dir
from the right, in turn, as long as each removal succeeds --
so
.B "rmdir \-p a/b/c"
removes
.BR c ,
then
.BR b ,
then
.BR a .
Stripping stops at the volume name (never attempted) or at the
first component that is not empty, whichever comes first; that
stop is reported and counts as a failure like any other.
.SH FILES
/usr/man/RMDIR  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
mkdir(1), rm(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 if every
.I dir
was removed, 1 if any operand failed, 2 on a usage error (no
operand given, or an unrecognised option).
.SH BUGS
None known.
